= Contributing to mediawiki.el =

This file describes how to build, test and change mediawiki.el.

'''AI agents:''' the canonical instructions for Claude Code, OpenCode, Qwen Code,
Gemini CLI and similar tools live in [[AGENTS.md]], which also carries the
release checklist.  Keep that file up to date instead of adding instructions
here.

== Project Overview ==

MediaWiki.el is an Emacs package for editing MediaWiki sites (like Wikipedia) directly from Emacs.  It requires Emacs 28.1 or later.  The current version is tracked in the <code>;; Version:</code> header of <code>mediawiki.el</code> and in <code>mediawiki-version</code> (<code>mediawiki-core.el</code>); the two must always match.

== Common Development Commands ==

=== Testing ===

* <code>make ci-test</code> - Run every suite, report all failures, exit non-zero if any failed.  This is what CI runs; use it before pushing.
* <code>make test</code> - Run every suite but keep going after failures
* <code>make test-mediawiki-simple</code> - Run essential functional tests (8 tests, quick verification)
* <code>make test-mediawiki-NAME</code> - Run a single test file, <code>tests/test-mediawiki-NAME.el</code>

At the time of writing there are 25 test files and roughly 386 tests.

=== Development Tasks ===

* <code>make autoloads</code> - Generate the autoloader file and byte-compile
* <code>make autoloads-only</code> - Generate the autoloader file only
* <code>make check-file FILE=filename.el</code> - Check a specific file for balanced parentheses
* <code>make editorconfig</code> - Clean up EOL and EOF whitespace
* <code>make clean</code> - Remove compiled files and artifacts

== Architecture ==

The package follows a modular architecture with these core modules:

=== Core Module Structure ===

* '''mediawiki.el''' - Main entry point with package metadata and requires all modules
* '''mediawiki-core.el''' - Core variables, constants, and fundamental utilities
* '''mediawiki-site.el''' - Site configuration and management
* '''mediawiki-faces.el''' - Font-lock face definitions for MediaWiki syntax
* '''mediawiki-font-lock.el''' - Font-lock keywords and syntax highlighting rules
* '''mediawiki-http.el''' - HTTP utilities (<code>url-http-get</code>, <code>url-http-post</code>) and compatibility functions
* '''mediawiki-api.el''' - MediaWiki API interaction and data processing
* '''mediawiki-auth.el''' - Password/clientlogin authentication
* '''mediawiki-oauth.el''' - OAuth 2.0 authentication
* '''mediawiki-page.el''' - Page editing, saving, and content management
* '''mediawiki-mode.el''' - Major mode definition, user interface, and <code>mediawiki-file-mode</code> for local files
* '''mediawiki-draft.el''' - Draft functionality and temporary editing
* '''mediawiki-completion.el''' - <code>completion-at-point</code> for wiki links
* '''mediawiki-history.el''' - Revision history browser
* '''mediawiki-diff.el''' - Revision diffs and follow-mode helpers
* '''mediawiki-watchlist.el''' - Watchlist browser
* '''mediawiki-user.el''' - User contributions
* '''mediawiki-discussion-tools.el''' - Discussion thread browser and replies
* '''mediawiki-support-desk.el''' - Support desk wrapper around <code>mediawiki-discussion-tools</code>
* '''mediawiki-utils.el''' - General utility functions

=== Key Design Principles ===

* Modular structure with clear separation of concerns
* Full backward compatibility maintained - users can still <code>(require 'mediawiki)</code> and access all functionality
* Each module handles a specific aspect of MediaWiki interaction
* Authentication uses Emacs auth-source library (supports encrypted password storage)
* Uses MediaWiki API for all server interactions

=== Testing Structure ===

* Tests are organized by module in <code>tests/</code> directory
* <code>test-mediawiki-simple.el</code> contains essential functional tests (always run these first)
* Each module has corresponding test file: <code>test-mediawiki-[module].el</code>
* Integration tests verify module interactions
* Extensive mocking to avoid network dependencies

== Important Implementation Notes ==

* Responses are JSON (<code>format=json</code>) parsed into alists; there is no XML path any more.
* <code>mediawiki-api-call</code> stringifies its arguments (<code>mediawiki-api--stringify-args</code>), so callers may pass integers for revision IDs, limits and namespaces.  Do not re-implement that coercion at call sites.
* Authentication for API calls is decided in <code>mediawiki-api-call</code>: an OAuth bearer header is added when the site is OAuth-configured, otherwise cookies from <code>mediawiki-do-login</code> are used.
* Tests must not hit the network (mock <code>mediawiki-api-call</code>, <code>url-http-post</code> or <code>url-retrieve</code>) and must not depend on the current date (build fixture timestamps relative to <code>(current-time)</code>).

== ChangeLog ==

Use <code>M-x add-change-log-entry</code>, or follow the existing format by hand, to document your changes in the [[ChangeLog]].

=== Dependencies ===

* Requires Emacs 28.1+
* Uses the built-in <code>url</code> library, with <code>mm-url</code> for form encoding
* Leverages auth-source for secure password and token management
* Uses ERT (Emacs Regression Testing) for test suite

=== Security Considerations ===

* Passwords should not be stored in plain text - the package will use auth-source if password is empty
* OAuth 2.0 is preferred over password login; secrets can also be kept in auth-source (see [[OAUTH-SETUP.org]])
* All network interactions go through MediaWiki API
* Authentication tokens are managed securely

=== Backward Compatibility ===

* All public functions from the original monolithic version remain available
* User configuration and customization variables unchanged
* Existing user workflows continue to work without modification

== Running Tests Effectively ==

# '''Quick verification''': Always start with <code>make test-mediawiki-simple</code> or the simple test runner to verify core functionality
# '''Full testing''': Use <code>make ci-test</code> for comprehensive validation
# '''Module-specific testing''': Individual test files can be run for focused debugging
# '''Test success metrics''': every suite must pass.  <code>make ci-test</code> exits non-zero when any suite fails, and that is the gate for merging and releasing.

== File Organization ==

* Root level contains all module <code>.el</code> files
* <code>tests/</code> directory contains comprehensive test suite with detailed README
* <code>Makefile</code> provides all development commands
* Documentation in MediaWiki format (<tt>.mediawiki</tt> files)
